				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "The Vault maintains two views of configuration data, #config (the raw input form) and #options (the structured ready to use form).\n\nTheVault performs a dual role, \n\n1) from the client end and 2) from the host/environment end.\n## 1) From the Client end\nA vault is empty by default and can be filled in.\n\na) A client class needs to be up and running easily\n\n`csClient := CloudsmithClient new.`\n\nAdding an api key ought to be as simple as.\n\n`csClient vault config at: #api_key put: 'csa_xyz'`\n## 2) From the Host Environment\nThe TheVault currentVault is populated from a world of env files, the osEnvironment and other useful things taking into consideration obfuscation of passwords, and multiple client configurations\nfor multiple apps and hosts.\n\nThe whole kitchen sink is in there.\nvault := TheVault currentVault\n\nWhen the vault is added to a client, the client gets an efficient copy, focusing on its own data.\n\nb) A fully configured client may be created by the factory class, the creation and configuration is negociated between teh factory and the client class. \n\nThe Client essentially chooses the form of the vault that it keeps, in the normal case\nall the data that is not client specific is discarded, in the client's local copy of the vault.\n\nWe have a tiered dictionary datastructure implemented as a linked list populated from a number of sources, {{gtClass:TTDictionaryTiered|show=comment|view}}  \n\n{{gtClass:TTVault}} Holds a master copy this data in its "
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
